{{Quote|Are you here to discipline me, you worm? Were you sent to stop me from reclaiming my ''former glory?'' I suppose I should be flattered that I am considered enough of a threat to be ''chastised'' by whomever employs you. But you will not stop me. Gardulla will ''rise again.''|translated=1|Gardulla|<ref name="Legacy2">[[Legacy of Vader 2|''Legacy of Vader'' 2]]</ref>}}
'''Gardulla Besadii the Elder''' was a [[Gender|female]] [[Besadii]] [[Hutt]] of the [[Hutt Clan]] [[Time|prior]] to and during the [[Clone Wars]]. Prior to the Clone Wars, Gardulla was the [[Slavery|owner]] of [[Shmi Skywalker Lars|Shmi]] and [[Anakin Skywalker]], but lost them to [[Watto]] in a bet.

==Biography==
{{Quote|How goes the war, gentlemen?|translated=1|Gardulla, to Obi-Wan Kenobi and Quinlan Vos|<ref name="HFZ" />}}
A [[Gender|female]] [[Hutt]] [[Reproduction|born]] on [[Nal Hutta]], Gardulla Besadii the Elder became a prominent member of the Besadii division of the [[Hutt Clan]] and was one of the most powerful Hutt [[crime lord]]s on [[Tatooine]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> [[Standard year|Years]] prior to the [[Invasion of Naboo]], Gardulla bought [[Shmi Skywalker Lars|Shmi Skywalker]] and her son [[Anakin Skywalker|Anakin]] as her [[Slavery|slaves]], however, she lost them in a [[Gambling|bet]] with the [[Toydarian]] [[junk dealer]] [[Watto]]<ref name="TPM" /> around [[38 BBY]]. In [[32 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> alongside [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba]], she watched as her former slave, Anakin Skywalker won the [[Boonta Eve Classic]] [[Podracing|podrace]] from Jabba's box seats.<ref name="TPM" />

[[File:Gardulla_with_Dancer.png|thumb|left|220px|Gardulla with a Twi'lek dancer]]
In [[21 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines" /> following [[Ziro Desilijic Tiure|Ziro]] the Hutt's [[Senate hostage crisis|breakout]] during the [[Clone Wars]], Gardulla and the [[Grand Hutt Council|Hutt Council]] met at [[Gardulla the Hutt's Palace|her palace]] on Nal Hutta and demanded that Ziro give up the [[Hutt Council records|Council's records]]. When [[Jedi Master]]s [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Quinlan Vos]] arrived, Gardulla asked them how the war was going and denied that the Hutts had anything to do with Ziro's escape or [[Cad Bane]]. When Vos accused her and the council of freeing Ziro, Gardulla said that he was lucky that the reasonable Kenobi was with him, or he would not be allowed to leave alive. Following that encounter, Gardulla and the Council discovered that Ziro had escaped. They then hired Bane to track Ziro down.<ref name="HFZ" />

Gardulla would live well past the other members of the Hutt Council, surviving<ref name="Legacy2" /> the slaughtering of the Council by [[Darth]] Vader<ref name="WOTB5">[[War of the Bounty Hunters 5|''War of the Bounty Hunters'' 5]]</ref> in [[3 ABY]]<ref name="Timelines" /> and Jabba's defeat via [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]]<ref name="ROTJ">{{Film|VI}}</ref> [[4 ABY|the following]] [[Standard year|year]].<ref name="Timelines" /> By [[34 ABY]],<ref name="LegacyDate">{{YouTube|video=0Mp3MNsQVDQ|text=The FUTURE of Star Wars Comics - An Interview With Charles Soule, Marc Guggenheim, and Alex Segura|channel=@StarWarsExplained|name=Star Wars Explained}} establishes that the events of ''[[Star Wars: Legacy of Vader]]'' take place immediately after the events of {{Film|VIII}}, which takes place in [[34 ABY]] per ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''.</ref> she lived in a [[Gardulla Besadii the Elder's fortress|fortress]] on Tatooine and plotted to reclaim her former glory. She acquired three [[rancor]]s alongside some [[Weequay]] guards to defend her fortress alongside a [[force-sensitive]] [[Unidentified Force-sensitive individual|creature]] who could stop a potential force user that may try to challenge her. Following [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren's]] ascension to [[Supreme Leader]] of the [[First Order]], the grandson of Vader was on a mission to learn more about Vader's legacy. With help from [[Vaneé]], Ren learned of his grandfather's enslavement by Gardulla and forcibly entered her fortress by killing her guards and rancors. When he requested an audience with the Hutt, she asked him why he had come to see her, flattered that she was of enough importance to be so violently approached. Ren stated that he was there for something she had done in the past, to which she responded asking to hear it, as revenge stories were something she enjoyed hearing. Ren said that she owned his grandfather when he was young, and she defended her actions by stating that slavery wasn't illegal in [[Hutt Space]] then or now. She then asked for her name, to which he threatened her and lit [[Kylo Ren's lightsaber|his lightsaber]]. She ordered her guards to fire on him, but Ren was able to take down all of them. That was when the force-sensitive creature in her court used [[telekinesis]] to take Ren's [[lightsaber]]. She told him that Skywalker's story was now his, and knocked him out and chained him in her prison.<ref name="Legacy2" /> 

However, using the power of the Force, Kylo Ren managed to break free from Gardulla's chains, destroy Gardulla's prison, and escape. After this, he went to the fortress of Gardulla<ref name="Legacy 3">[[Legacy of Vader 3|''Legacy of Vader'' 3]]</ref> where he [[Death|killed]] the Hutt<ref name="Legacy 12">[[Legacy of Vader 12|''Legacy of Vader'' 12]]</ref> and her guards, before he gave an order to the First Order to destroy Gardulla's fortress.<ref name="Legacy 3" />

==Personality and traits==
Gardulla was a female Hutt crime lord, who sat on the Hutt Council. She was 3.7 [[meter]]s (12 [[Foot|feet]], 2 inches) long.<ref name="Join the Battle" /> She had [[Color|yellow]] [[eye]]s and green-tan skin.<ref name="TPM" /> Gardulla had palaces on [[Gardulla Besadii the Elder's fortress|Tatooine]] as well as her [[Planet|homeworld]] of Nal Hutta.<ref name="Join the Battle" /> She owned Shmi and Anakin Skywalker as slaves, until she lost them in a wager to the junk dealer Watto.<ref name="TPM" />

==Skills and abilities==
As an esteemed member of the Hutt Council, Gardulla was known for her skills as a leader, as well as in persuasion and intimidation.<ref name="Join the Battle" />

